      <Comment source="BioCyc">This reaction is catalyzed by the aci-reductone dioxygenase enzyme, ARD&apos;, but it can also occur by non-enzymatic spontaneous oxidation in the presence of air |CITS: [7852397]|. It is not known whether the reaction occurs non-enzymatically in vivo |CITS: [7852397]|. The non-enzymatic oxidation 1,2-dihydroxy-3-keto-5-methylthiopentene anion is partially inhibited by catalase |CITS: [8227039][7852397]|. This reaction is catalyzed by the aci-reductone dioxygenase enzyme, ARD&apos;, but it can also occur by non-enzymatic spontaneous oxidation in the presence of air |CITS: [7852397]|. It is not known whether the reaction occurs non-enzymatically in vivo |CITS: [7852397]|. The non-enzymatic oxidation 1,2-dihydroxy-3-keto-5-methylthiopentene anion is partially inhibited by catalase |CITS: [8227039][7852397]|. If Ni(2+) is bound instead of Fe(2+), the reaction catalyzed by EC 1.13.11.53 occurs instead. The enzyme from Klebsiella oxytoca (formerly Klebsiella pneumoniae) ATCC 8724 is involved in the methionine salvage pathway.</Comment>
